[Event "KIA vs the French"]

{The King's Indian Attack is a system: e4, d3, Nd2, Ngf3, g3, Bg2, O-O, Re1. White attacks on the kingside with e5 and h4.}
1. e4 {Centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
1... e6 {The French. The pawn on e6 controls d5.}
2. d3 {[%csl Ge4] The KIA: avoid the French theory.}
2... d5 {Centre. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on e4.}
 (2... c5 {Black delays ...d5. The pawn on c5 controls d4.}
3. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls d4 and e5.}
3... Nc6 {Develops. The knight on c6 controls d4 and e5.}
4. g3 {Same KIA setup: Bg2, O-O, Re1.}
)
3. Nd2 {Supports e4.}
3... Nf6 {Develops. The knight on f6 eyes the pawn on e4.}
4. Ngf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls d4 and e5.}
4... c5 {Space. The pawn on c5 controls d4.}
5. g3 {Fianchetto.}
5... Nc6 {Develops. The knight on c6 controls d4 and e5.}
6. Bg2 {The bishop on the long diagonal.}
6... Be7 {Develops.}
7. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
7... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
8. Re1 {[%csl Ge5] Supports e5.}
8... b5 {The queenside attack begins.}
 (8... Qc7 {Black adds pressure to e5 in advance. The queen on c7 eyes the pawn on g3 and controls e5.}
9. Qe2 {[%csl Ge5] Over-protects e5 before pushing.}
)
9. e5 {[%cal Ge5f6] Kicks the knight and gains kingside space.}
9... Nd7 {Retreats. The knight on d7 eyes the pawn on e5.}
10. Nf1 {[%csl Gh2,Gg3] The knight heads for h2 or g3 to support h4–h5.} *

[Event "KIA vs the Sicilian & Caro-Kann"]

{The same setup works against 1...c5 and 1...c6.}
1. e4 {Centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
1... c5 {The Sicilian. The pawn on c5 controls d4.}
 (1... c6 {The Caro-Kann. The pawn on c6 controls d5.}
2. d3 {The KIA approach.}
2... d5 {Centre. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on e4.}
3. Nd2 {Supports e4.}
3... e5 {Black builds a centre. The pawn on e5 controls d4.}
4. Ngf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 eyes the pawn on e5 and controls d4.}
4... Bd6 {Develops.}
5. g3 {Fianchetto.}
5... Nf6 {Develops. The knight on f6 eyes the pawn on e4.}
6. Bg2 {Long diagonal.}
6... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
7. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
7... Re8 {Supports ...e4 ideas and e5.}
8. Re1 {Supports e4; e4xd5 or Qe2 next.}
)
2. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls d4 and e5.}
2... e6 {Flexible. The pawn on e6 controls d5.}
 (2... Nc6 {Develops. The knight on c6 controls d4 and e5.}
3. d3 {KIA setup.}
3... g6 {Closed-Sicilian style fianchetto.}
4. g3 {Mirrors.}
4... Bg7 {Long diagonal. The bishop on g7 eyes the pawn on b2 and controls d4 and e5.}
5. Bg2 {Long diagonal.}
)
3. d3 {The KIA setup.}
3... Nc6 {Develops. The knight on c6 controls d4 and e5.}
4. g3 {Fianchetto.}
4... d5 {Centre. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on e4.}
5. Nbd2 {Supports e4.}
5... Nf6 {Develops. The knight on f6 eyes the pawn on e4.}
6. Bg2 {Long diagonal.}
6... Be7 {Develops.}
7. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
7... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
8. Re1 {[%csl Ge5] Prepares e5.} *
